; Limit 09: runtime code shipped as a library cannot call the program's main.
; Blocks job 7. A runtime written in L0 would be linked into every program the
; way lib/prelude.l0 is: as the prelude group of spec section 7.1. A call in a
; prelude declaration resolves only to prelude functions, so the entry point
; cannot reach main. Putting the runtime in the program group instead makes
; every runtime helper name collide with the user's definitions.
;
; This file is the runtime; 09-library-entry-program.l0 is the program. They
; must be compiled as a bundle with this file as the prelude, which
; tools/l0check cannot express. See 09-library-entry.out.txt.

(def l0_entry ((input (list int))) (list int)
  (main input))
